# Keep the build context to what the compiler actually needs. Everything here
# would otherwise be copied into a build layer and cached — including secrets.

bin/
tmp/
.git/
.github/

# The local EVM stand. 315 MB of artifacts, cache and node_modules that the Go
# build has no use for, and which would otherwise be uploaded as build context
# and kept in the shared build cache.
hardhat/

# The real configuration carries API keys and the database URL. It never reaches
# the final image (only the binary is copied forward), but it would land in a
# build layer and in the shared build cache. It is mounted at runtime instead.
config.json
config.*.json
!config.example.json

Dockerfile*
docker-compose.yml
.dockerignore

.claude/
*.md

# NOTE: schema/ is deliberately NOT ignored — schema/embed.go compiles the .sql
# into the binary so the image can create its own tables.
